<p>Iran has launched a new mechanism to regulate vessel traffic through the Strait of Hormuz, requiring ships to receive emailed transit rules from an address linked to the Persian Gulf Strait Authority and obtain permission before crossing, Iranian state-run Press TV reported on May 5. Tehran and Washington continued to make competing assertions over control of one of the world’s main energy chokepoints.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SnkEZ9sxMHpBVjBrN3gWQzaZdj3zkOm6eS8tgJaivNYiDu4m4S4xogaNDLJL5wrjuqqoBVM2lui9tbSogAB7CIvDQ_JinOrdGg2qJhYTFxRQ_I89FKBuws0-0gPDAkdZPtdcbUEMiFZsKKMzrjVWhHeecxSSRoVMSLdGMzLQ5KTl7ELnMaBKX8KnmjnwVwluukFvviJFlCYDrgdm-SW3fS2EeZB8u9xG' alt='A billboard in Tehran last week, depicting a closed Strait of Hormuz over the mouth of President Trump.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Transit rules: Kurier reported that it was initially unclear what the detailed transit rules required and how Iran would respond to violations.</li><li>Ceasefire dispute: Aaj TV reported that Tehran had earlier signaled willingness to reopen the strait after a Pakistan-mediated ceasefire involving the United States, Israel and Lebanon, then declared it closed again over alleged truce violations.</li><li>Draft legislation: A draft bill advancing in Iran’s parliament would ban Israeli-affiliated vessels, impose severe restrictions on ships linked to the United States and other “hostile” countries, and create tolls for non-hostile ships.</li><li>Map caveat: Several Czech reports said Press TV described an expanded Iranian control map for the strait but did not publish the map itself.</li></ul><blockquote>Iran is fully aware of the situation, and the current conditions will not be tolerable for the United States - Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian state media: Press TV described the rollout as part of tighter security after U.S. escalation and said the U.S. blockade effort had failed. (<a href='https://presstv.ir/Detail/2026/05/05/768114/Iran-activates-new-Strait-of-Hormuz-transit-system,-tightening-security-amid-US-escalation'>Press TV</a>)</li><li>Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps: The IRGC Navy warned that the only safe route through the strait was the corridor Iran had announced and said ships using other routes risked decisive intervention. (<a href='https://www.haber7.com/dunya/haber/3625568-irandan-son-dakika-hurmuz-bogazi-karari-yeni-gelismeyi-resmen-duyurdular'>Haber7</a>)</li><li>United States government: Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said the United States had control of the strait and would escort trapped ships out, while Iran said it controlled the waterway. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000010883344/trump-iran-strait-of-hormuz.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump said he would suspend Project Freedom for a short time while officials checked whether a U.S.-Iran agreement could be completed and signed. (<a href='https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/iran-kuendigt-mechanismus-fuer-transit-durch-strasse-von-hormuz-an/403157106'>Kurier</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/05/05/world/iran-war-trump-hormuz/iran-announces-a-new-system-for-traffic-in-the-strait-of-hormuz'>Iran announces a new system for traffic in the Strait of Hormuz.</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/no-mail-no-passage-iran-launches-new-system-to-regulate-hormuz-shipping-11455780#publisher=newsstand'>No Mail, No Passage: Iran Launches New System To Regulate Hormuz Shipping</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-war-west-asia-conflict-ceasefire-talks-strait-of-hormuz-issue-live-updates-may-6-2026/article70945447.ece'>Iran-Israel war LIVE: Iran enforces new &#x27;sovereign&#x27; transit rules in Strait of Hormuz; mandates prior permits for vessels</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/iran-se